      "message": "[warning] Line 131: Setting `wantedState.applied \u003d true` when the current endpoint already matches can make this wanted state permanently inert. If Telecom later changes the current endpoint away from the requested one and `onCallEndpointChanged` re-emits, this same wanted state will now hit `if (wantedState.applied) return@subscribe` and will not restore the requested endpoint. If the wanted state is meant to remain the latest desired route, only skip the current match without marking it applied, or reset `applied` when the current endpoint changes away from the target. For example:\n```suggestion\n                            if (currentEndpoint?.identifier \u003d\u003d endpoint.identifier) return@subscribe\n                            if (wantedState.applied) return@subscribe\n```",
